WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.930
A visitor told our school: the morning

2
00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:05.110
class does better than the afternoon

3
00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:08.110
class, so afternoon lessons should end.

4
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:09.760
The averages agreed.

5
00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.460
But the averages were hiding something.

6
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.760
Today: how to read data claims carefully,

7
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.440
and how to keep pupils' data private.

8
00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:22.050
We looked inside the groups.

9
00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:24.610
The afternoon class had most of the

10
00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:27.090
pupils who joined this year, and many

11
00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.230
were still learning English.

12
00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.910
Within each group, the two

13
00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:32.610
classes scored about the same.

14
00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:36.740
So the time of day was not the cause.

15
00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:38.930
Two things can go together

16
00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:40.670
without one causing the other.

17
00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.690
Before you act on a pattern, ask:

18
00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.590
what else could explain it?

19
00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.490
Be careful with small groups too.

20
00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:51.600
A class of eight can swing a lot

21
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.120
from one test to the next.

22
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:57.070
One good or bad day changes the average.

23
00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.040
Look at several tests before you judge.

24
00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:01.940
Now privacy.

25
00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:04.770
When we share results, we share the

26
00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:06.770
class picture, not one person.

27
00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.510
Marks, health and family

28
00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:10.930
details stay private.

29
00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:13.660
A ranked list on the wall can

30
00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:14.980
hurt someone for years.

31
00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:18.810
Use pupil numbers instead of names.

32
00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:21.870
Collect only what your question needs.

33
00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:25.400
Keep the list of names locked away, and

34
00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:27.080
delete the data when you are done.

35
00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:28.770
Quick check!

36
00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:31.220
Pupils who eat breakfast at

37
00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:32.800
school get better marks.

38
00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:35.270
Does that prove breakfast

39
00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:36.610
causes better marks?

40
00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:38.780
Not on its own.

41
00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:40.810
Pupils who come early for

42
00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:42.730
breakfast may also miss fewer

43
00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:44.970
lessons, or live closer to school.

44
00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.200
Breakfast may well help, but the

45
00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.940
pattern alone does not prove it.

46
00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:53.210
A fair test would compare similar pupils.

47
00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:56.970
In the app, open the bias lab.

48
00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.760
See how data that leaves out a group

49
00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.580
gives unfair answers, and how fixing

50
00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:03.800
the data changes them.

51
00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:05.470
Your turn.

52
00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:07.380
Your class wants to show

53
00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:09.040
parents how it did in a test.

54
00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:11.520
What is the safest thing to share?

55
00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:15.520
The class average and spread, not names.

56
00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:19.000
Remember: look inside the groups, ask

57
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.280
what else could explain a pattern, and

58
00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:23.160
be careful with small groups.

59
00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.010
Share the class, never the child.

60
00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:30.130
Try it yourself: find one claim with a

61
00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:31.890
number in an advert or a post.

62
00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:35.130
Ask what else could explain it, and what

63
00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:37.470
data would check it, before you share it.
